Oh.

243
00:14:35,332 --> 00:14:36,500
Sorry, but I'm not the only one.

244
00:14:36,584 --> 00:14:38,460
- Yes, I see.
- That helps. Thank you.

245
00:14:38,544 --> 00:14:41,589
I wonder which person
everyone can relate to the most.

246
00:14:41,672 --> 00:14:44,508
Honestly, I feel like
I can relate to all of them.

247
00:14:44,592 --> 00:14:46,719
- Oh! Impressive.
- Sensei. Of course she can.

248
00:14:46,802 --> 00:14:48,721
I'm a monster at understanding people.

249
00:14:48,804 --> 00:14:50,723
- That's amazing.
- An empathy monster?

250
00:14:50,806 --> 00:14:54,393
I mean, look, there's no way
Hikaru could choose just one person.

251
00:14:54,476 --> 00:14:57,354
And when it comes to whether
she can truly trust Tai-chan…

252
00:14:57,438 --> 00:14:58,272
Yeah.

253
00:14:58,355 --> 00:15:01,984
…she must be scared of being betrayed,
especially with her past trauma.

254
00:15:02,067 --> 00:15:03,569
I mean, her mindset is,

255
00:15:03,652 --> 00:15:06,196
- she's here to find someone to marry.
- She is. And, Bo was…

256
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:08,782
- Yeah?
- …pretty low on her list,

257
00:15:08,866 --> 00:15:11,827
but he moved up,
so he's probably feeling good about that.

258
00:15:11,911 --> 00:15:12,828
Yeah.

259
00:15:12,912 --> 00:15:15,706
But Ari thought he was way up here,
and then he got dropped.

260
00:15:15,789 --> 00:15:18,208
- Totally see what you're saying.
- That's why he's so upset.

261
00:15:18,292 --> 00:15:22,254
- Makes sense. It must be tough for him.
- But then, Hikaru, she just can't

262
00:15:22,338 --> 00:15:23,714
make up her mind, right?

263
00:15:23,797 --> 00:15:25,716
Exactly. That's why she started crying.

264
00:15:25,799 --> 00:15:28,135
- Oh.
- You know, sometimes that happens.

265
00:15:28,218 --> 00:15:30,763
You can be so popular, it makes you cry.

266
00:15:30,846 --> 00:15:33,307
- Too-popular tears.
- Too-popular tears.

267
00:15:33,390 --> 00:15:35,851
Have either of you cried
from being too popular?

268
00:15:35,935 --> 00:15:38,979
- Not me. But sensei has, right?
- You haven't? I bet you have.

269
00:15:39,063 --> 00:15:41,106
- Uh…
- I think that's a yes.

270
00:15:41,190 --> 00:15:42,733
Oh, my gosh!

271
00:15:49,114 --> 00:15:52,910
<i>Today, we're going to learn</i>
<i>about Okinawan culture.</i>

272
00:15:52,993 --> 00:15:53,911
TSUNAMI CENTER

273
00:15:53,994 --> 00:15:54,870
That one?

274
00:15:56,288 --> 00:15:57,915
Nice to meet you.

275
00:15:57,998 --> 00:15:58,832
MS. HARUKO

276
00:15:58,916 --> 00:16:00,250
- Hello.
- Looks nice.

277
00:16:00,334 --> 00:16:02,503
- Please have a seat.
- Oh, okay.

278
00:16:02,586 --> 00:16:04,630
- Hello.
- Please sit wherever you like.

279
00:16:04,713 --> 00:16:05,881
- Yes, hello.
- How are you?

280
00:16:05,965 --> 00:16:06,924
I'm good.

281
00:16:07,007 --> 00:16:10,469
- It smells like a friend's house.
- Love these chairs. So nostalgic.

282
00:16:10,552 --> 00:16:12,680
- We can sit anywhere?
- Should I sit here?

283
00:16:12,763 --> 00:16:13,722
I'm sitting here.

284
00:16:13,806 --> 00:16:14,974
Hello, everyone.

285
00:16:15,057 --> 00:16:16,433
- Hello.
- Morning.

286
00:16:16,517 --> 00:16:17,810
Aren't you all adorable?

287
00:16:17,893 --> 00:16:19,520
- That's so kind.
- So kind.

288
00:16:19,603 --> 00:16:21,522
As for the origin
of this instrument, the <i>shamisen…</i>

289
00:16:21,605 --> 00:16:22,481
MS. AZAMA

290
00:16:22,564 --> 00:16:24,775
…it began during the war
when people had nothing.

291
00:16:24,858 --> 00:16:27,903
They used empty cans left behind
by the US military,

292
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:30,447
hoping to use the instrument
to raise their spirits.

293
00:16:31,031 --> 00:16:34,827
In Okinawa, and this is true
for most households, including ours,

294
00:16:34,910 --> 00:16:38,163
there's usually a <i>shamisen</i>
in the <i>tokonoma </i>alcove.

295
00:16:38,247 --> 00:16:40,708
Through this experience,
I hope you'll get a chance

296
00:16:40,791 --> 00:16:43,544
to feel and get a sense
of the <i>shamisen </i>for yourselves.

297
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:45,963
ASHIBI SHONGANE

298
00:16:46,046 --> 00:16:49,341
<i>I'm pining</i>

299
00:16:49,425 --> 00:16:55,931
<i>I'm pining for your love</i>

300
00:16:59,184 --> 00:17:00,060
That's all.

301
00:17:01,186 --> 00:17:02,813
- Pow, pow, pow!
- Thank you very much.

302
00:17:02,896 --> 00:17:03,939
- Awesome.
- Thank you.

303
00:17:04,023 --> 00:17:06,400
But is he being genuine,
or is that sarcasm?

304
00:17:06,483 --> 00:17:09,153
I know, right? It looks like
he's trying to be tough.

305
00:17:09,945 --> 00:17:12,906
This song is called "Ashibi Shongane."

306
00:17:12,990 --> 00:17:18,120
This song is about when you are out,
having fun, you should never forget about…

307
00:17:18,662 --> 00:17:20,748
- The one you love?
- …your boyfriend or girlfriend.

308
00:17:20,831 --> 00:17:23,625
Haven't you ever felt like
you just can't stop thinking about them,

309
00:17:23,709 --> 00:17:24,710
all day and night?

310
00:17:25,335 --> 00:17:27,254
- Yes, I have.
- You have?

311
00:17:27,337 --> 00:17:28,630
- Yes.
- How lovely.

312
00:17:29,298 --> 00:17:30,799
- Definitely.
- Lucky you.

313
00:17:33,844 --> 00:17:34,845
Okay, like this.

314
00:17:34,928 --> 00:17:38,223
Tun, ten, tun. Right.

315
00:17:38,307 --> 00:17:40,350
Tun, ten, tun.

316
00:17:40,851 --> 00:17:42,519
- I hold it like this?
- Hold it down like this.

317
00:17:42,603 --> 00:17:43,854
MARIRIN (25)
BAR WORKER

318
00:17:43,937 --> 00:17:46,774
Put your other finger here,
then play the middle string.

319
00:17:47,274 --> 00:17:48,442
- Like this?
- Yeah, that's it!

320
00:17:48,525 --> 00:17:49,359
See, I got this.

321
00:17:50,736 --> 00:17:53,322
- Okay, I'm gonna try.
- Your nails are cute.

322
00:17:54,281 --> 00:17:55,491
- Hmm?
- Those nails are cute.

323
00:17:55,574 --> 00:17:56,658
Not too long?

324
00:17:56,742 --> 00:17:58,077
- Not long enough.
- Really?

325
00:17:58,160 --> 00:17:59,870
They'd look even better longer.

326
00:17:59,953 --> 00:18:01,413
I just noticed your nose is pierced.

327
00:18:01,497 --> 00:18:02,664
- You didn't know?
- I didn't know.

328
00:18:02,748 --> 00:18:05,834
- Just now? In this moment?
- I've just noticed. I like it.

329
00:18:06,794 --> 00:18:08,504
- You don't like it?
- No, I like it.

330
00:18:08,587 --> 00:18:09,421
- For real?
- Yeah.

331
00:18:13,592 --> 00:18:16,011
- <i>Ooh, watch out.</i>
- <i>She's pissed.</i>

332
00:18:20,057 --> 00:18:22,017
I liked getting
to play the <i>sanshin.</i>

333
00:18:22,101 --> 00:18:23,685
I didn't think it'd be so hard.

334
00:18:24,561 --> 00:18:26,605
- So classy!
- Guys sat down first?

335
00:18:26,688 --> 00:18:27,606
Jeez, okay.

336
00:18:27,689 --> 00:18:29,942
You guys are sitting
in super awkward spots.

337
00:18:31,026 --> 00:18:31,902
Fine.

338
00:18:32,611 --> 00:18:34,071
- So?
- Hey, wait a sec.

339
00:18:37,908 --> 00:18:39,993
- I'll sit here.
- I'll sit right here then.

340
00:18:40,077 --> 00:18:43,455
<i>Oh, next to him.</i>
<i>Hikaru's looking more vulnerable now.</i>

341
00:18:45,457 --> 00:18:47,626
Please, no.
I have a bad feeling about this.

342
00:18:47,709 --> 00:18:50,129
- I have too.
- <i>They've become negative.</i>

343
00:18:50,212 --> 00:18:51,046
<i>Oh, for sure.</i>

344
00:18:51,130 --> 00:18:53,215
- <i>Time for the sauna.</i>
- <i>Oh.</i>

345
00:18:53,298 --> 00:18:55,843
<i>The person who has been</i>
<i>selected for the sauna</i>

346
00:18:55,926 --> 00:18:57,928
<i>is someone who hasn't been in yet.</i>

347
00:19:00,305 --> 00:19:01,140
<i>It's Ari.</i>

348
00:19:01,223 --> 00:19:02,307
- Wow.
- Why me?

349
00:19:02,391 --> 00:19:03,684
- What?
- What?

350
00:19:04,268 --> 00:19:07,980
<i>Please choose the one</i>
<i>that you'd like to go to the sauna with.</i>

351
00:19:12,359 --> 00:19:13,360
Who will he pick?

352
00:19:13,443 --> 00:19:15,612
- Tough spot for him.
- Exactly.

353
00:19:15,696 --> 00:19:17,489
This is a big moment for Ari.

354
00:19:18,699 --> 00:19:19,700
Can I say it now?

355
00:19:20,617 --> 00:19:22,035
I'm going with Maririn.

356
00:19:22,786 --> 00:19:24,079
- Off you go.
- Me?

357
00:19:24,746 --> 00:19:25,581
Okay.

358
00:19:26,248 --> 00:19:27,082
Huh?

359
00:19:28,167 --> 00:19:29,626
Whoa.

360
00:19:30,210 --> 00:19:31,628
- Let's go.
- Yeah.

361
00:19:31,712 --> 00:19:32,713
My second time.

362
00:19:33,463 --> 00:19:35,048
- Really?
- Yep, it is.

363
00:19:43,682 --> 00:19:47,769
REFRESHED

364
00:19:49,146 --> 00:19:49,980
Hey there.

365
00:19:50,647 --> 00:19:52,191
- It's so bright.
- I know.

366
00:19:52,941 --> 00:19:55,110
- Can we just walk in like this?
- Yeah.

367
00:19:55,194 --> 00:19:56,153
Coming in.

368
00:19:57,321 --> 00:19:58,822
- Thanks for having me.
- Such a party guy.

369
00:19:58,906 --> 00:20:00,866
- What? Am I?
- Total party guy.

370
00:20:00,949 --> 00:20:02,784
- I'm going all out, for real.
- Oh, sorry.

371
00:20:02,868 --> 00:20:04,536
This is great. Whoa, it's so warm.

372
00:20:05,204 --> 00:20:07,623
So, were you happy
when I invited you to the sauna?

373
00:20:07,706 --> 00:20:09,499
- Yeah, totally. I love saunas.
- For real?

374
00:20:09,583 --> 00:20:10,500
For sure.

375
00:20:10,584 --> 00:20:12,794
- Okay, cool.
- I mean, I like your personality too.

376
00:20:14,504 --> 00:20:15,464
- You do?
- Mmm. Yeah.

377
00:20:16,048 --> 00:20:18,425
So, you could see
a potential romantic connection?

378
00:20:18,508 --> 00:20:19,968
- Oh, yeah, for sure.
- Really?

379
00:20:20,052 --> 00:20:21,637
I never thought
you felt that way about me.

380
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:23,472
- So I'm just super surprised.
- Yeah, I get that.

381
00:20:23,555 --> 00:20:24,932
I didn't mean to surprise you.

382
00:20:25,015 --> 00:20:28,810
I guess I wanted to see what the vibe was,
and get a sense of how you feel about me.

383
00:20:29,853 --> 00:20:33,815
I like that you're direct.
You told Hikaru how you felt, straight up.

384
00:20:33,899 --> 00:20:37,527
I think that's nice, the way you express
your feelings like that.

385
00:20:37,611 --> 00:20:38,487
I feel like

386
00:20:38,570 --> 00:20:42,324
most people I've been with never told me
they liked me with such directness.

387
00:20:42,407 --> 00:20:45,535
So, yeah, I was actually
kind of jealous of her.

388
00:20:47,537 --> 00:20:50,749
Honestly, I thought you just asked me out

389
00:20:50,832 --> 00:20:52,751
just to mess with Hikaru's feelings.

390
00:20:52,834 --> 00:20:53,710
Oh, no, not at all.

391
00:20:54,711 --> 00:20:58,465
Well, if you're coming at me like that,
of course I'd see you that way.

392
00:21:01,051 --> 00:21:03,136
Yeah. I'd switch into that mode for sure.

393
00:21:03,220 --> 00:21:04,179
Romance mode?

394
00:21:04,763 --> 00:21:06,765
Wait, what? What was that look?

395
00:21:06,848 --> 00:21:09,643
- Maririn is cute too.
- True, she is cute.

396
00:21:09,726 --> 00:21:12,187
- And I think he's starting to notice that.
- Oh, right, right.

397
00:21:14,022 --> 00:21:16,191
- What happened?
- Mmm.

398
00:21:17,025 --> 00:21:19,236
- I have no idea.
- It's probably nothing.

399
00:21:19,319 --> 00:21:22,990
Then why did he pick someone else?
I was sure he'd pick you, Hikaru.

400
00:21:23,490 --> 00:21:24,783
Hmm, guess you never know.

401
00:21:24,866 --> 00:21:26,952
- Nothing is ever guaranteed.
- True.

402
00:21:27,452 --> 00:21:32,165
Why is Hikaru acting like that
when you've been showing so much love?

403
00:21:32,249 --> 00:21:34,501
Apparently she can't see me
as a romantic option.

404
00:21:34,584 --> 00:21:37,796
- Oh, yeah? She sees you as a friend?
- Yeah, she could only see me as a friend.

405
00:21:37,879 --> 00:21:38,714
Mmm.

406
00:21:38,797 --> 00:21:40,674
But she said
she'd try to see me differently.

407
00:21:40,757 --> 00:21:43,093
- Hearing that is a turnoff, you know?
- Mmm-hmm.

408
00:21:43,176 --> 00:21:44,469
- Makes me feel over it.
- Yeah.

409
00:21:44,553 --> 00:21:46,930
But with you, it feels like
you accept me for who I am.

410
00:21:48,765 --> 00:21:51,268
Well, I think
that's just normal, honestly.

411
00:21:52,769 --> 00:21:54,062
- Yeah. Mmm-hmm.
- Of course.

412
00:21:55,272 --> 00:21:58,900
But if that's how you feel about me,
then I want to acknowledge that.

413
00:22:01,611 --> 00:22:02,446
Yeah.

414
00:22:03,447 --> 00:22:06,575
Hmm, I guess
I want you to see the real me.

415
00:22:06,658 --> 00:22:10,078
I want to be more open with you,
so you can see more of what's inside.

416
00:22:10,162 --> 00:22:11,663
And I want to get to know you better.

417
00:22:14,416 --> 00:22:16,418
- Mmm-hmm. Got it.
- If I'm being honest.

418
00:22:16,501 --> 00:22:18,837
I understand.
This is kind of embarrassing.

419
00:22:18,920 --> 00:22:20,547
- I wasn't expecting that.
- No. Why wouldn't I?

420
00:22:21,923 --> 00:22:25,052
- I wanted to be straight with you.
- Mmm, yeah, I like straightforward people.

421
00:22:25,969 --> 00:22:27,179
It's a good quality.

422
00:22:29,556 --> 00:22:31,058
- Really?
- Yeah, really.

423
00:22:31,141 --> 00:22:31,975
Good to know.

424
00:22:33,143 --> 00:22:35,771
- I have that wassup energy.
- Oh, really? Oh nice.

425
00:22:35,854 --> 00:22:38,398
No one believes me
when I say that, but that's how I am.

426
00:22:38,482 --> 00:22:41,234
- I get super hyped.
- Okay, let's do a quick sync then.

427
00:22:41,318 --> 00:22:43,153
Let's see if
I can feel that vibe you felt.

428
00:22:43,236 --> 00:22:45,238
- What do you mean?
- Let's see.

429
00:22:45,322 --> 00:22:47,032
- What are you doing?
- Okay. I see.

430
00:22:47,115 --> 00:22:49,368
- Did you feel the "wassup"?
- Yeah, it hit me pretty hard.

431
00:22:49,451 --> 00:22:50,452
You felt the "wassup"?

432
00:22:50,535 --> 00:22:52,662
It was like an electric shock,
or something.

433
00:22:52,746 --> 00:22:56,083
Like 100,000 volts, or more like
1.2 million volts of lightning.

434
00:22:56,166 --> 00:22:58,168
- Mmm.
- Let's have a quick hug.

435
00:22:58,251 --> 00:22:59,294
- Sure. Now?
- Wow!

436
00:22:59,378 --> 00:23:01,046
- Yeah.
- Oh, okay.

437
00:23:01,129 --> 00:23:03,048
- Whoa! Oh, my gosh!
- My face.

438
00:23:03,131 --> 00:23:04,758
- My face, it's a mess.
- Oh, sorry.

439
00:23:04,841 --> 00:23:06,093
- I'll stop.
- My makeup came off.

440
00:23:06,176 --> 00:23:08,136
- <i>Nice, Ari is back.</i>
- Okay, like that.

441
00:23:12,265 --> 00:23:13,850
Man, I'm so embarrassed.

442
00:23:18,438 --> 00:23:20,690
- Was that uncomfortable?
- That was funny. I'm not uncomfortable.

443
00:23:20,774 --> 00:23:22,442
- Really? Are we good?
- I would tell you.

444
00:23:22,526 --> 00:23:24,694
- Sorry.
- Is my face a mess? Do I look okay?

445
00:23:24,778 --> 00:23:26,947
- You look fine. You look gorgeous.
- No, no.

446
00:23:27,030 --> 00:23:28,490
- I'm dead serious.
- For real?

447
00:23:28,573 --> 00:23:29,574
Mmm-hmm.

448
00:23:37,165 --> 00:23:38,708
Mr. Wassup is back.

449
00:23:39,584 --> 00:23:41,670
- Welcome back.
- I'm back, y'all!

450
00:23:41,753 --> 00:23:44,631
Wassup!

451
00:23:47,008 --> 00:23:49,636
It was seriously the best.

452
00:23:52,389 --> 00:23:54,391
- He was in tears earlier.
- I know, right?

453
00:23:56,518 --> 00:23:59,229
I was like, she's got
such a big heart, you know?

454
00:23:59,312 --> 00:24:01,440
She's direct, and meets me where I'm at.

455
00:24:01,523 --> 00:24:03,066
- Mmm, mmm, mmm.
- Yeah.

456
00:24:03,150 --> 00:24:05,485
And actually,
we ended up hugging each other.

457
00:24:06,069 --> 00:24:08,655
- I definitely felt the chemistry.
- You hugged in the sauna?

458
00:24:08,738 --> 00:24:09,656
- Yeah.
- Whoa.

459
00:24:09,739 --> 00:24:10,699
What?

460
00:24:10,782 --> 00:24:14,911
And, she said something in there
that blew my mind.

461
00:24:16,163 --> 00:24:17,330
She was like, "Guess what?"

462
00:24:18,373 --> 00:24:20,083
She said, "I'm into the 'wassup.'"

463
00:24:22,127 --> 00:24:24,337
Ari, you're good at building up a story.

464
00:24:24,421 --> 00:24:26,715
- A killer payoff.
- I was like, "Wait, what?"

465
00:24:26,798 --> 00:24:28,592
She knows "wassup," huh?

466
00:24:28,675 --> 00:24:30,594
For real, so I said,
"Let me check your vibes."

467
00:24:30,677 --> 00:24:33,180
I was like, "You ready?"

468
00:24:33,263 --> 00:24:36,641
And when we did this,
I swear I felt a jolt of electricity.

469
00:24:36,725 --> 00:24:39,436
Brr! Like that.

470
00:24:39,519 --> 00:24:40,479
What an idiot.

471
00:24:40,562 --> 00:24:41,396
KAZU-KUN (29)

472
00:24:41,480 --> 00:24:44,691
- Like, I gotta know more about this girl.
- You're such an idiot.

473
00:24:44,774 --> 00:24:45,692
He's sweet.

474
00:24:45,775 --> 00:24:47,611
- Yeah, so cute.
- He is.

475
00:24:47,694 --> 00:24:48,528
BAD BITCH

476
00:24:48,612 --> 00:24:49,488
You're back!

477
00:24:49,571 --> 00:24:50,947
- Here she is.
- Hey.

478
00:24:51,031 --> 00:24:52,574
- I'm finally back.
- Welcome back.

479
00:24:52,657 --> 00:24:56,453
- <i>She looks happy.</i>
- The sauna was awesome, to be honest.

480
00:24:57,662 --> 00:24:59,956
He was like, "I just want to have
a real conversation with you,

481
00:25:00,040 --> 00:25:03,126
since we haven't yet."
And he opened up to me, a lot.

482
00:25:03,793 --> 00:25:06,630
Basically, I was the first one here
who was sweet to him.

483
00:25:06,713 --> 00:25:09,007
And he liked that,
and wanted to let me know.

484
00:25:09,090 --> 00:25:10,800
- Mmm-hmm.
- That felt good.

485
00:25:11,468 --> 00:25:13,053
- I feel refreshed.
- Good.

486
00:25:15,764 --> 00:25:19,059
- Fact that he picked Maririn was a twist.
- I did not see that coming.

487
00:25:19,142 --> 00:25:22,145
- He wanted to move on, I think.
- Mmm. Yeah.

488
00:25:22,229 --> 00:25:24,689
So, you don't think he was trying
to make Hikaru jealous?

489
00:25:24,773 --> 00:25:27,567
That might have been
what he was trying to do at first.

490
00:25:27,651 --> 00:25:28,527
Right.

491
00:25:28,610 --> 00:25:32,197
But in the end, I think he felt
Maririn's warmth, and fell for her.

492
00:25:32,280 --> 00:25:34,241
- <i>Her warmth and acceptance.</i>
- <i>Right.</i>

493
00:25:34,324 --> 00:25:37,327
<i>Yeah, he started laughing,</i>
<i>like he was able to relax again.</i>

494
00:25:37,410 --> 00:25:40,413
There is something about saunas,
they bring people closer.

495
00:25:40,497 --> 00:25:42,749
- Yeah, it's the sweat.
- Steam and sweat get your blood flowing.

496
00:25:42,832 --> 00:25:45,210
Blood flow? I'm learning
so much about anatomy from you.

497
00:25:45,293 --> 00:25:48,171
When blood starts flowing more,
your heart rate goes up.

498
00:25:48,255 --> 00:25:51,341
- Right.
- And that creates a visceral sensation.

499
00:25:51,424 --> 00:25:53,009
- I see.
- Like, "Could this be love?"

500
00:25:53,093 --> 00:25:55,303
- Is my heart racing because I'm in love?
- Right.

501
00:25:55,387 --> 00:25:58,306
Or is it friggin' hot in here, that it?

502
00:25:58,390 --> 00:26:00,308
- Leo's face was so supportive.
- It was.

503
00:26:00,392 --> 00:26:02,811
- He's a good guy.
- Yeah, like a dad. Yeah.

504
00:26:02,894 --> 00:26:04,187
Like, "Good for you, son."

505
00:26:04,271 --> 00:26:07,566
<i>- Like a dad watching his son play sports.</i>
- <i>A total dad right there.</i>

506
00:26:07,649 --> 00:26:09,442
- Isn't he younger though?
- Wait, he is?

507
00:26:09,526 --> 00:26:10,402
Younger than Ari?

508
00:26:22,080 --> 00:26:23,957
<i>It is time for Ethics class.</i>

509
00:26:25,125 --> 00:26:29,129
<i>The two transfer students will share</i>
<i>their family backgrounds,</i>

510
00:26:29,212 --> 00:26:31,715
<i>someone they want to apologize to,</i>

511
00:26:31,798 --> 00:26:37,012
<i>as well as any major mistakes they feel</i>
<i>that they've made in their life so far.</i>

512
00:26:37,095 --> 00:26:39,222
<i>First up is Ha-chan.</i>

513
00:26:40,181 --> 00:26:41,933
- Let's go.
- Okay, here I go.

514
00:26:47,522 --> 00:26:49,566
So, I'll start with how I grew up.

515
00:26:49,649 --> 00:26:52,235
When I was in first grade,
my parents got divorced.

516
00:26:52,861 --> 00:26:54,070
My siblings and I were split up,

517
00:26:54,154 --> 00:26:56,364
and I went back and forth
between my mom's and my dad's.

518
00:26:56,448 --> 00:26:57,407
HA-CHAN (27)
TRAINER

519
00:26:57,490 --> 00:27:01,077
I also went to a child guidance center,
and stayed at a children's home.

520
00:27:01,703 --> 00:27:06,041
Then, when I was in sixth grade,
I went to live with my dad.

521
00:27:06,666 --> 00:27:09,794
There was a new mother figure, my stepmom.

522
00:27:11,296 --> 00:27:15,050
I'd grown up feeling like
I never had a real parent in my life.

523
00:27:16,843 --> 00:27:18,470
That feeling was so strong

524
00:27:19,179 --> 00:27:22,891
that I wasn't able to get along
with my dad's new wife either.

525
00:27:23,892 --> 00:27:26,186
At first, she told me to call her "Mom."

526
00:27:26,269 --> 00:27:28,480
But I just couldn't bring myself
to say it.

527
00:27:30,065 --> 00:27:32,609
And then, she said something shocking,

528
00:27:32,692 --> 00:27:34,861
"I can't raise this kid anymore."

529
00:27:40,659 --> 00:27:43,328
If it were your own child,
no matter how hard it gets,

530
00:27:44,371 --> 00:27:46,206
you'd still take care of your child.

531
00:27:46,289 --> 00:27:48,541
That's when I knew she'd abandon me.

532
00:27:49,334 --> 00:27:52,128
From then on, I hated her.
Like, "Who does she think she is?"

533
00:27:52,879 --> 00:27:54,881
I just couldn't accept her as my mother.

534
00:27:56,633 --> 00:28:00,470
Our fights got so bad that she eventually
came at me with a kitchen knife.

535
00:28:00,553 --> 00:28:02,806
How can I describe it?
I was covered in blood.

536
00:28:02,889 --> 00:28:05,392
She didn't stab me,
they were more like small cuts.

537
00:28:08,687 --> 00:28:10,522
I couldn't tell
if it was from losing blood,

538
00:28:10,605 --> 00:28:14,275
or maybe it was just the smell of blood,
but I passed out.

539
00:28:14,359 --> 00:28:16,611
When I woke up, I knew I had to leave.

540
00:28:17,654 --> 00:28:19,489
So I moved in with my older brother.

541
00:28:20,782 --> 00:28:23,827
I started working at a hostess bar
when I was around 19.

542
00:28:24,411 --> 00:28:28,456
Then, I tried martial arts on a whim.
As soon as I started, I felt like, "Wow.

543
00:28:29,457 --> 00:28:31,918
This actually makes me feel so alive."

544
00:28:32,001 --> 00:28:34,003
And that's pretty much my story
up until now.

545
00:28:34,087 --> 00:28:34,963
MA-KUN (28)
MMA FIGHTER

546
00:28:35,046 --> 00:28:35,880
And…

547
00:28:36,756 --> 00:28:40,552
the person
I feel like I want to apologize to

548
00:28:41,344 --> 00:28:43,221
is my stepmom.

549
00:28:45,515 --> 00:28:47,559
To give you a bit more context,

550
00:28:47,642 --> 00:28:51,104
in my first year of junior high,
my dad was diagnosed with cancer

551
00:28:51,187 --> 00:28:53,064
and told he had five years to live.

552
00:28:53,982 --> 00:28:55,859
His wife was doing her best
to support him.

553
00:28:56,693 --> 00:28:58,695
She searched all over Japan,

554
00:28:59,571 --> 00:29:04,242
looking for treatments that didn't require
insurance, and different foods,

555
00:29:04,325 --> 00:29:06,911
all to give my dad a chance at survival.

556
00:29:07,912 --> 00:29:10,165
And now, he's still alive,

557
00:29:10,790 --> 00:29:13,418
and it is all because of her.

558
00:29:16,796 --> 00:29:20,759
When I realized just how much
she had done to support my dad,

559
00:29:22,051 --> 00:29:23,595
I finally respected her.

560
00:29:24,304 --> 00:29:26,139
But I never could say sorry.

561
00:29:27,682 --> 00:29:30,643
So I want to apologize to my stepmom.

562
00:29:31,686 --> 00:29:33,772
Thank you.

563
00:29:35,607 --> 00:29:38,401
Whenever I ask married people
if marriage is worth it,

564
00:29:38,485 --> 00:29:41,738
I feel like about 90% of them
tell me stuff like,

565
00:29:41,821 --> 00:29:43,406
"No, it's not worth it,"

566
00:29:43,490 --> 00:29:46,993
"Marriage is tough,"
or, "It's not that great."

567
00:29:47,076 --> 00:29:49,621
There are so many people like that
in Japan.

568
00:29:50,455 --> 00:29:52,040
But when your dad was sick,

569
00:29:52,123 --> 00:29:55,668
his wife took the time to look up
hospitals all around the country,

570
00:29:55,752 --> 00:29:57,253
and took care of his meals.

571
00:29:58,254 --> 00:29:59,714
And it just makes me wonder,

572
00:29:59,798 --> 00:30:03,551
how many women in this world would go
that far for their husbands, you know?

573
00:30:05,094 --> 00:30:07,222
And it made me envy your dad so much.

574
00:30:07,305 --> 00:30:09,808
I want to be with a woman
who's that devoted to me,

575
00:30:09,891 --> 00:30:12,268
and I want to devote myself to her.

576
00:30:12,352 --> 00:30:13,812
I don't know if that's mutual love,

577
00:30:13,895 --> 00:30:16,815
but that's the kind
of relationship I want.

578
00:30:17,690 --> 00:30:18,650
RURU (26)
MODEL

579
00:30:18,733 --> 00:30:20,652
When I was young, my mom would say,

580
00:30:20,735 --> 00:30:24,155
"You know what?
I wish I had never given birth to you."

581
00:30:24,239 --> 00:30:27,075
So even though our situations
are a little different,

582
00:30:27,158 --> 00:30:31,079
I still remember how painful it was
to hear something like that as a child.

583
00:30:31,162 --> 00:30:33,331
I think that's something
you and I have in common.

584
00:30:35,333 --> 00:30:40,922
After going through such a painful past,
you were able to find martial arts.

585
00:30:41,005 --> 00:30:44,217
And I think it's amazing
that you have something,

586
00:30:44,300 --> 00:30:48,304
even just one thing, that you can
pour yourself into, and feel alive.

587
00:30:50,098 --> 00:30:54,978
In that sense, after hearing your story,
I feel like I respect you so much now.

588
00:30:55,562 --> 00:30:58,940
I mean, let's be honest,
when you first came here,

589
00:30:59,023 --> 00:31:00,859
we had some disagreements, remember?

590
00:31:01,776 --> 00:31:04,153
But hearing your story today
made me realize

591
00:31:04,237 --> 00:31:07,240
that you and I experienced a similar past.

592
00:31:07,323 --> 00:31:10,410
So, now I want to be more open
and get to know you more.

593
00:31:11,327 --> 00:31:13,121
Thank you.

594
00:31:14,622 --> 00:31:16,958
- She's great.
- Wow.

595
00:31:17,041 --> 00:31:19,085
It's admirable that she shared that.

596
00:31:19,919 --> 00:31:21,671
<i>Next up is Kazu-kun.</i>

597
00:31:23,047 --> 00:31:23,965
<i>Kazu-kun.</i>

598
00:31:24,048 --> 00:31:26,426
- <i>Yeah, Kazu-kun is hard to read.</i>
- <i>He is.</i>

599
00:31:26,509 --> 00:31:27,969
<i>He is a complete mystery.</i>

600
00:31:28,469 --> 00:31:30,847
My family history is pretty complicated.

601
00:31:31,431 --> 00:31:34,642
Basically, I was passed back and forth
between my two parents.

602
00:31:35,143 --> 00:31:37,437
And my dad was very abusive.

603
00:31:38,479 --> 00:31:42,066
So I moved around between
relatives' places and children's homes.

604
00:31:42,775 --> 00:31:45,361
Eventually, in junior high,

605
00:31:47,071 --> 00:31:48,031
I got arrested.

606
00:31:48,114 --> 00:31:50,992
- What did you get arrested for?
- I mean, you know how it is.

607
00:31:51,576 --> 00:31:53,912
If you don't hang
with the right crew, you're a loser.

608
00:31:53,995 --> 00:31:54,829
Mmm.

609
00:31:54,913 --> 00:31:57,415
If they think you're
chickening out or you're scared,

610
00:31:57,999 --> 00:32:00,043
you get pushed aside, right away.

611
00:32:00,126 --> 00:32:02,086
And you become the one getting bullied.

612
00:32:02,170 --> 00:32:04,672
So I got to a point where
I couldn't back out anymore.

613
00:32:05,173 --> 00:32:07,675
And one time,
my friends were playing with fire.

614
00:32:09,010 --> 00:32:10,386
I thought that was lame.

615
00:32:10,970 --> 00:32:13,014
But, still, I ended up setting someone…

616
00:32:14,015 --> 00:32:15,141
on fire.

617
00:32:15,224 --> 00:32:16,100
Yeah.

618
00:32:16,184 --> 00:32:17,560
And then, like,

619
00:32:17,644 --> 00:32:21,189
three days after that, I got busted, so…

620
00:32:21,814 --> 00:32:22,649
Mmm.

621
00:32:24,025 --> 00:32:24,901
It was wrong.

622
00:32:28,154 --> 00:32:29,405
And I regret it.

623
00:32:30,657 --> 00:32:32,825
You know that photo pinned to the mailbox?

624
00:32:33,368 --> 00:32:34,661
How old were you in that?

625
00:32:35,370 --> 00:32:37,747
I think I was around 15, maybe.

626
00:32:38,456 --> 00:32:40,917
- You look like a hardcore yankii there.
- Yeah.

627
00:32:41,000 --> 00:32:43,169
- It's that iron perm. Right?
- An iron perm. Yeah.

628
00:32:43,252 --> 00:32:45,380
I'd add a headband
and go straight to work,

629
00:32:47,006 --> 00:32:49,342
So I got busted, and when I got out,

630
00:32:50,468 --> 00:32:52,679
I worked outdoor labor jobs back home.

631
00:32:53,513 --> 00:32:55,598
I'd mostly been living on my own.

632
00:32:56,557 --> 00:32:57,433
And then,

633
00:32:58,059 --> 00:33:01,270
I moved to Tokyo and worked as a host,
still living on my own.

634
00:33:02,021 --> 00:33:05,775
I never relied on anyone,
I never asked anyone for their help.

635
00:33:07,402 --> 00:33:09,821
I mean, I was too proud back then.

636
00:33:09,904 --> 00:33:13,574
And in terms of my apology,
I want to apologize to my dad.

637
00:33:15,034 --> 00:33:17,078
I was 17 when I moved to Tokyo,

638
00:33:17,662 --> 00:33:20,039
but I had already cut ties
with him before that.

639
00:33:20,123 --> 00:33:22,542
I left home
after a pretty stupid argument,

640
00:33:22,625 --> 00:33:25,670
and from then on,
I just decided to ignore him.

641
00:33:26,170 --> 00:33:28,965
Even when he made an effort
to reach out to me,

642
00:33:29,048 --> 00:33:30,466
I'd just snap at him like,

643
00:33:30,550 --> 00:33:32,510
"It's too late to start acting
like a dad now."

644
00:33:33,011 --> 00:33:37,682
But the next time I saw him,
he wasn't able to move his body anymore.

645
00:33:39,600 --> 00:33:43,271
And that was the first time
I felt regret about it.

646
00:33:47,608 --> 00:33:50,278
I got a phone call.
"Your dad just passed away."

647
00:33:51,029 --> 00:33:53,740
Seriously, when I got the call,
I was like,

648
00:33:53,823 --> 00:33:55,825
"I don't care. That's not my problem."

649
00:33:56,659 --> 00:33:59,120
But they said, "Come anyway. Come home."

650
00:33:59,620 --> 00:34:02,081
"If you don't come,
we'll cremate him without you.

651
00:34:02,165 --> 00:34:05,251
"But if you come first thing tomorrow,
we'll keep him here,

652
00:34:05,334 --> 00:34:06,669
and keep him presentable."

653
00:34:07,336 --> 00:34:10,673
When I saw him, I cried more
than I ever had in my entire life.

654
00:34:15,678 --> 00:34:17,555
I cried for about ten hours.

655
00:34:17,638 --> 00:34:20,683
I was overwhelmed by regret,
and so many pent up feelings.

656
00:34:23,394 --> 00:34:26,773
And so, since it had been a while
since he'd passed away,

657
00:34:26,856 --> 00:34:29,025
they couldn't keep him there much longer.

658
00:34:29,734 --> 00:34:32,278
So about half a day after I arrived,

659
00:34:33,404 --> 00:34:34,447
he was cremated.

660
00:34:35,281 --> 00:34:36,616
He'd been in such poor health,

661
00:34:36,699 --> 00:34:39,744
there were hardly any bones left
after he was cremated.

662
00:34:39,827 --> 00:34:41,537
There was nothing left for me
to take home.

663
00:34:50,379 --> 00:34:51,339
That's my story.

664
00:34:52,256 --> 00:34:53,424
I feel so much regret.

665
00:34:54,842 --> 00:34:59,097
I wish I'd had a drink with him.
Like, "This is how I'm doing now,"

666
00:34:59,180 --> 00:35:00,598
or "I'm working hard."

667
00:35:00,681 --> 00:35:02,767
I never got to tell him things like that.

668
00:35:05,019 --> 00:35:07,021
It's really strange, you know.

669
00:35:07,105 --> 00:35:11,400
In that moment, what I remembered
were the things he did for me,

670
00:35:11,484 --> 00:35:13,820
the fun times,
and the times when he was kind.

671
00:35:14,529 --> 00:35:16,739
All those times when
he was yelling, or being abusive,

672
00:35:16,823 --> 00:35:18,908
I didn't think about that,
not for a second.

673
00:35:18,991 --> 00:35:21,661
I thought about the fun times
when my dad made me laugh…

674
00:35:21,744 --> 00:35:23,121
DAD - KAZU-KUN

675
00:35:23,204 --> 00:35:25,581
…the food he cooked for me,
the breakfasts he made.

676
00:35:25,665 --> 00:35:29,335
The places we went together,
the car, even the smells,

677
00:35:29,418 --> 00:35:32,338
all those things
came back to me so vividly.

678
00:35:33,297 --> 00:35:35,466
I usually think crying is embarrassing,

679
00:35:36,175 --> 00:35:38,928
but, in that moment, I didn't care at all.

680
00:35:39,804 --> 00:35:40,972
I cried my eyes out.

681
00:35:42,932 --> 00:35:44,934
But since I hadn't seen him for so long,

682
00:35:45,643 --> 00:35:49,605
sometimes I think, "Maybe the real him
is still alive somewhere out there."

683
00:35:50,940 --> 00:35:53,693
I guess, no matter what,
they're still your parents.

684
00:35:54,485 --> 00:35:58,990
No matter how hurtful they are,
when they die, it's still sad.

685
00:35:59,740 --> 00:36:02,743
Yeah. And that's why
you cried so much, Kazuma.

686
00:36:03,870 --> 00:36:05,621
Even if you're not the crying type.

687
00:36:06,622 --> 00:36:09,667
It makes me think that it's the parents
who are loved unconditionally,

688
00:36:09,750 --> 00:36:10,835
not the kids.

689
00:36:10,918 --> 00:36:13,045
Some kids never get loved
by their parents.

690
00:36:13,546 --> 00:36:16,924
But somehow, parents are
always loved by their kids.

691
00:36:18,968 --> 00:36:21,554
For the people in your life,
you should remember,

692
00:36:22,763 --> 00:36:24,849
a moment will come
when you can't see them anymore.

693
00:36:26,392 --> 00:36:27,977
So while you can still see them,

694
00:36:28,728 --> 00:36:31,814
you need to stay in touch,
and tell them how you feel.

695
00:36:32,398 --> 00:36:33,983
Eight.

696
00:36:34,567 --> 00:36:35,401
Awesome.

697
00:36:37,320 --> 00:36:40,114
I felt like I saw
Kazuma's warm, human side.

698
00:36:41,449 --> 00:36:45,369
It doesn't seem like he shows
that side of himself very often,

699
00:36:45,453 --> 00:36:47,997
but he's been through a lot, in his past.

700
00:36:48,664 --> 00:36:54,295
I've been wanting to apologize to a parent
as well, so I related to that a lot.

701
00:36:55,296 --> 00:36:58,341
When I was little,
my mom worked in the nightlife industry,

702
00:36:58,841 --> 00:37:00,927
and there was no one to look after me.

703
00:37:01,010 --> 00:37:02,637
My dad wasn't around either.

704
00:37:02,720 --> 00:37:05,389
So, I was always being left
with a babysitter at night.

705
00:37:05,473 --> 00:37:09,227
I never got along with my mom,
and I would run away from home a lot.

706
00:37:09,310 --> 00:37:12,480
But in life, whenever I mess up
in some big way,

707
00:37:12,563 --> 00:37:15,733
my mom is the one
who's ultimately there for me.

708
00:37:15,816 --> 00:37:19,403
I've finally realized that
over the past few years.

709
00:37:19,487 --> 00:37:22,907
My mom is so important to me now,
and I want to be there for her.

710
00:37:23,407 --> 00:37:25,743
After hearing their stories today,

711
00:37:25,826 --> 00:37:28,663
I felt that I needed to be honest

712
00:37:28,746 --> 00:37:31,749
and tell her everything
that I've been feeling lately.

713
00:37:42,260 --> 00:37:43,970
<i>Ah, the phone.</i>

714
00:37:45,054 --> 00:37:46,722
- <i>I'm already nervous.</i>
- <i>Right?</i>

715
00:38:09,662 --> 00:38:10,579
<i>Hello?</i>

716
00:38:11,122 --> 00:38:13,249
Hello. Mom?

717
00:38:13,916 --> 00:38:14,792
It's Ruru.

718
00:38:15,793 --> 00:38:17,128
<i>You okay?</i>

719
00:38:17,211 --> 00:38:18,921
It's been a while.

720
00:38:19,755 --> 00:38:23,467
I just realized that
I've never told you how I feel.

721
00:38:23,551 --> 00:38:25,386
<i>What? Where's this coming from?</i>

722
00:38:26,846 --> 00:38:30,516
Well, you know, you were a single parent,
and always working.

723
00:38:30,599 --> 00:38:32,226
- And, you were…
<i>- Yeah.</i>

724
00:38:32,310 --> 00:38:34,687
…working so hard,
you even coughed up blood.

725
00:38:35,313 --> 00:38:37,982
You kept running your snack bar.

726
00:38:38,065 --> 00:38:38,983
<i>Yeah.</i>

727
00:38:39,066 --> 00:38:43,487
And I had to spend my nights
at that… daycare.

728
00:38:43,571 --> 00:38:47,283
And during that time,
you were also being abused.

729
00:38:47,366 --> 00:38:48,326
<i>Yeah.</i>

730
00:38:48,409 --> 00:38:51,579
We even had to run away together,
barefoot. Remember?

731
00:38:51,662 --> 00:38:52,580
<i>Yeah.</i>

732
00:38:53,372 --> 00:38:57,418
Because of that, I guess I started feeling
some resentment toward you.

733
00:38:57,501 --> 00:38:58,586
<i>Mmm-hmm.</i>

734
00:38:58,669 --> 00:39:02,548
Every time we talked,
we'd just end up fighting.

735
00:39:02,631 --> 00:39:03,716
<i>Mmm.</i>

736
00:39:03,799 --> 00:39:06,010
We butted heads, in so many ways.

737
00:39:06,093 --> 00:39:07,386
<i>Yeah.</i>

738
00:39:07,470 --> 00:39:10,598
But you're the most important person
to me.

739
00:39:10,681 --> 00:39:13,142
I'm sorry for making you cry
so many times,

740
00:39:14,101 --> 00:39:15,853
for making you worry so much…

741
00:39:16,520 --> 00:39:19,899
…and for not being
a daughter you could be proud of.

742
00:39:20,649 --> 00:39:22,151
<i>That's not true.</i>

743
00:39:22,234 --> 00:39:25,363
<i>I was happy to pick you up in the morning,</i>

744
00:39:25,446 --> 00:39:28,074
<i>and that joy kept me going through</i>
<i>the long nights at work.</i>

745
00:39:28,157 --> 00:39:28,991
Mmm-hmm.

746
00:39:29,075 --> 00:39:33,162
<i>Even as a single mom working</i>
<i>all the time, I still loved you so much.</i>

747
00:39:33,245 --> 00:39:35,414
<i>As a mother,</i>
<i>I wanted to support you financially.</i>

748
00:39:35,498 --> 00:39:38,376
<i>But I'm sorry</i>
<i>I couldn't raise you in a way</i>

749
00:39:39,085 --> 00:39:41,754
<i>that let you know you were loved.</i>

750
00:39:50,888 --> 00:39:52,765
I want to be totally honest now.

751
00:39:54,308 --> 00:39:56,977
I'm happy that you're my mom.
I'm glad you had me.

752
00:39:57,061 --> 00:39:58,396
<i>Aw.</i>

753
00:39:58,479 --> 00:40:00,314
Mmm. From now on, I want to show you

754
00:40:00,398 --> 00:40:02,775
all the love I wasn't able
to show you before.

755
00:40:03,442 --> 00:40:06,529
<i>Don't make me cry.</i>
<i>I'll get so embarrassed.</i>

756
00:40:08,197 --> 00:40:10,032
<i>I should be saying that to you.</i>

757
00:40:11,534 --> 00:40:14,453
<i>Thank you for choosing</i>
<i>to have me as your mother.</i>

758
00:40:15,371 --> 00:40:17,957
<i>I am so honored to get a call like this.</i>

759
00:40:20,000 --> 00:40:22,294
<i>You are my greatest treasure. </i>

760
00:40:25,714 --> 00:40:28,008
<i>Money isn't what matters. </i>

761
00:40:28,092 --> 00:40:30,636
- It's about us, Mom.
<i>- Yeah.</i>

762
00:40:30,719 --> 00:40:32,763
<i>It's is all about kids and their parents.</i>

763
00:40:32,847 --> 00:40:35,015
<i>Money is not what matters in this world.</i>

764
00:40:35,099 --> 00:40:36,684
<i>You taught me that.</i>

765
00:40:36,767 --> 00:40:39,186
<i>- Screw money, it's about us.</i>
- It's about us.

766
00:40:40,729 --> 00:40:42,731
<i>- I get it now.</i>
- Let's talk more soon.

767
00:40:42,815 --> 00:40:44,692
<i>- Yeah, let's talk more often.</i>
- Yeah. Sure.

768
00:40:44,775 --> 00:40:46,944
<i>- Let's grab a beer together soon.</i>
- Yeah, let's do that.

769
00:40:47,027 --> 00:40:48,529
<i>- Yeah, okay?</i>
- Okay. Thank you.

770
00:40:48,612 --> 00:40:49,697
<i>Give it your all out there.</i>

771
00:40:49,780 --> 00:40:51,574
- I'll do my best.
<i>- Until the very end.</i>

772
00:40:51,657 --> 00:40:52,575
- Bye.
<i>- Bye now.</i>

773
00:40:52,658 --> 00:40:53,784
- Thank you.
<i>- All right.</i>

774
00:40:53,868 --> 00:40:54,702
Good night.

775
00:41:16,307 --> 00:41:18,392
- That was so moving.
- It was.

776
00:41:18,476 --> 00:41:20,269
- She's such a wonderful mom.
- Yeah.

777
00:41:20,352 --> 00:41:21,228
- Right?
- Mmm.

778
00:41:21,312 --> 00:41:25,774
After hearing Kazu-kun
and Ha-chan's stories, Ruru was inspired.

779
00:41:25,858 --> 00:41:28,986
- Yeah. They inspired her, for sure.
- She took their words to heart.

780
00:41:29,069 --> 00:41:32,239
- That call was great for her mom, right?
- Yes. Absolutely.

781
00:41:32,323 --> 00:41:36,619
I think parent-child relationships
are often the root of deep trauma

782
00:41:36,702 --> 00:41:39,330
that we sometimes carry
into other relationships.

783
00:41:39,830 --> 00:41:43,792
Actually, I've had
very similar conversations with my mom.

784
00:41:43,876 --> 00:41:45,377
- Oh, really?
- And with my dad.

785
00:41:45,461 --> 00:41:48,005
I'll call out of nowhere and say,
"Okay, interview time." Yeah.

786
00:41:48,589 --> 00:41:49,715
What?

787
00:41:49,798 --> 00:41:51,509
I ask things like, "How did you grow up?"

788
00:41:51,592 --> 00:41:53,636
or, "What were
your past relationships like?"

789
00:41:53,719 --> 00:41:56,055
- Oh, wow.
- Or "How did you meet Dad?"

790
00:41:56,138 --> 00:41:57,932
Or "What were your relationships like

791
00:41:58,015 --> 00:41:59,308
- before Dad?"
- You ask that?

792
00:41:59,391 --> 00:42:00,351
- Wow.
- I do.

793
00:42:00,434 --> 00:42:01,977
- Really?
- And honestly it's so…

794
00:42:02,061 --> 00:42:03,896
What's the word? Therapeutic for me.

795
00:42:03,979 --> 00:42:04,939
- Truly is.
- I see.

796
00:42:05,022 --> 00:42:06,565
Did that make you closer to your parents?

797
00:42:06,649 --> 00:42:08,108
Absolutely. We're super close.

798
00:42:08,192 --> 00:42:09,443
Much closer than before.

799
00:42:09,527 --> 00:42:10,361
- I see.
- Wow.

800
00:42:10,444 --> 00:42:12,154
Way closer than we used to be.

801
00:42:12,238 --> 00:42:14,698
"Money isn't what matters.
It's about us, Mom."

802
00:42:15,282 --> 00:42:16,617
- Those were powerful words.
- Right?

803
00:42:16,700 --> 00:42:17,993
I was completely blown away.

804
00:42:18,077 --> 00:42:19,870
I thought it was all about money.

805
00:42:19,954 --> 00:42:22,122
- Huh?
- That's why it hit me so hard.

806
00:42:22,206 --> 00:42:24,500
- Until this moment?
- Right up until this very moment.

807
00:42:24,583 --> 00:42:27,294
- You thought the world's all about money?
- The world is all about money.

808
00:42:27,378 --> 00:42:29,463
Take a break.
Can you take your break early?

809
00:42:30,047 --> 00:42:32,716
- Go ahead and take your break.
- You're making me take a break?

810
00:42:32,800 --> 00:42:34,885
Assun said something important, yeah?

811
00:42:34,969 --> 00:42:37,263
"Children can't help loving
their parents."

812
00:42:37,346 --> 00:42:39,682
- She did say that, yeah.
- That was an amazing line.

813
00:42:39,765 --> 00:42:41,433
Of course parents are

814
00:42:41,517 --> 00:42:44,520
supposed to love their children,
but sometimes they can't.

815
00:42:44,603 --> 00:42:46,605
- Those parents are out there.
- Yeah, they are.

816
00:42:46,689 --> 00:42:48,607
It was so profound, but she said it

817
00:42:48,691 --> 00:42:50,693
- so casually, you know?
- That was a great line.

818
00:42:50,776 --> 00:42:53,904
SMOKERS' LOUNGE

819
00:42:59,326 --> 00:43:01,787
- <i>What's going on?</i>
- <i>He's got something on his mind.</i>

820
00:43:03,664 --> 00:43:05,666
<i>Didn't things get awkward with him before?</i>

821
00:43:05,749 --> 00:43:07,543
<i>Yeah, with Assun, right?</i>

822
00:43:17,511 --> 00:43:21,098
I've been more upfront than you
about my feelings.

823
00:43:23,434 --> 00:43:25,853
Forget what I just said. I made a mistake.

824
00:43:46,957 --> 00:43:49,918
- Thanks for that.
- Yeah, it'll go faster with two of us.

825
00:43:50,002 --> 00:43:51,211
- Absolutely.
- Mmm-hmm.

826
00:43:55,466 --> 00:43:56,884
Oh, right. Here.

827
00:43:58,552 --> 00:43:59,637
- What?
- Read it later.

828
00:43:59,720 --> 00:44:00,804
- Read it later?
- Yeah.

829
00:44:00,888 --> 00:44:02,598
- You're giving it to me now?
- Yeah.

830
00:44:24,662 --> 00:44:25,663
"DEAR ASUKA,"

831
00:44:25,746 --> 00:44:27,748
"FIRST OF ALL, THANK YOU FOR EVERYTHING."

832
00:44:27,831 --> 00:44:30,834
"MY FEELINGS FOR YOU ARE ALL TRUE,
AND IT WON'T CHANGE."

833
00:44:30,918 --> 00:44:33,295
"EVEN IF NEW PEOPLE COME,
OR IF WE GO BACK TO THE OUTSIDE WORLD,

834
00:44:33,379 --> 00:44:35,381
I ONLY CARE ABOUT YOU,
AND YOU HAVE MY WORD."

835
00:44:50,979 --> 00:44:52,189
- Hey.
- Ari.

836
00:44:52,272 --> 00:44:53,816
Hey, how's it going?

837
00:44:53,899 --> 00:44:55,401
- How have you been?
- How are you?

838
00:44:55,484 --> 00:44:57,861
- Me?
- I mean, to be completely honest,

839
00:44:57,945 --> 00:44:59,905
- Yeah?
- I thought you would pick Hikaru.

840
00:45:00,572 --> 00:45:01,407
- For the sauna?
- Yeah.

841
00:45:01,490 --> 00:45:02,408
Oh.

842
00:45:02,491 --> 00:45:05,285
- You're always so upfront with her.
- Ah.

843
00:45:05,369 --> 00:45:08,122
So when you picked Marina,
I was like, "What?" You know?

844
00:45:08,205 --> 00:45:11,250
- You were like, "What?"
- And I couldn't stop staring at Hikaru.

845
00:45:11,333 --> 00:45:13,252
Like "What's going on? What happened?"

846
00:45:13,836 --> 00:45:16,422
- I just wanted to pick Maririn.
- Oh, I see.

847
00:45:16,505 --> 00:45:18,590
The way things are going,
even if I picked Hikaru again,

848
00:45:18,674 --> 00:45:20,551
- it probably wouldn't change anything.
- Right.

849
00:45:21,051 --> 00:45:23,762
Besides, I was actually getting
a little curious about Maririn,

850
00:45:23,846 --> 00:45:25,139
so I just decided to ask her out.

851
00:45:25,222 --> 00:45:26,974
- Mmm, I see.
- Yeah.

852
00:45:27,599 --> 00:45:28,976
And Hikaru barely talks to me.

853
00:45:29,059 --> 00:45:31,979
So, I didn't want to ask her out again
and make her think I was fine with her

854
00:45:32,062 --> 00:45:34,273
- taking me for granted.
- Hikaru should take the initiative.

855
00:45:34,356 --> 00:45:36,692
- So I was like, whatever.
- Mmm.

856
00:45:37,276 --> 00:45:40,237
Yeah, and I talked to Maririn,
and I think she's definitely cool.

857
00:45:40,320 --> 00:45:43,449
- Marina's great, seriously.
- Plus, honestly, during our chat,

858
00:45:43,949 --> 00:45:47,745
I got the feeling Maririn is a little
more ready to find love while she's here.

859
00:45:47,828 --> 00:45:48,829
Totally, yeah.

860
00:45:48,912 --> 00:45:50,998
- Just from the sauna.
- Yeah, that's true.

861
00:45:51,081 --> 00:45:54,501
If you're seriously here to fall in love,
then a woman with that same mindset

862
00:45:54,585 --> 00:45:56,962
- is definitely better for you.
- Yeah. Of course.

863
00:45:58,005 --> 00:45:59,506
- I know.
- Don't you think?

864
00:45:59,590 --> 00:46:01,717
- I'll take this away.
- Sounds good.

865
00:46:01,800 --> 00:46:03,051
- What's this?
- This?

866
00:46:03,135 --> 00:46:05,345
- Definitely not.
- It'll work. Go ahead.

867
00:46:06,054 --> 00:46:07,473
Yeah.

868
00:46:07,556 --> 00:46:10,350
Girl on the second day
of her period is no joke.

869
00:46:11,351 --> 00:46:14,354
Wait, did I hear her right?

870
00:46:14,438 --> 00:46:16,523
She said exactly
what I thought she said, yeah?

871
00:46:16,607 --> 00:46:18,734
Yes. They really don't hold anything back.

872
00:46:19,735 --> 00:46:22,112
- Need to talk?
- Yes please. Definitely.

873
00:46:28,452 --> 00:46:30,871
Have you been able to sort out
your thoughts?

874
00:46:30,954 --> 00:46:32,414
- Even a little?
- Not at all.

875
00:46:32,498 --> 00:46:34,333
Not at all, huh?

876
00:46:34,416 --> 00:46:37,211
I think it's time for me
to stop saying "I don't know."

877
00:46:37,294 --> 00:46:39,880
Yeah, you should stop saying that.
It'll work out.

878
00:46:40,798 --> 00:46:42,549
Just let yourself go with the flow.

879
00:46:42,633 --> 00:46:43,550
Exactly.

880
00:46:45,093 --> 00:46:45,969
What?

881
00:46:46,804 --> 00:46:48,889
- Did I say something wise?
- You did, yeah.

882
00:46:50,432 --> 00:46:52,017
<i>Bo is cute.</i>

883
00:46:52,893 --> 00:46:54,603
I wonder if I can fall in love.

884
00:46:56,188 --> 00:46:58,440
You're the only one
who can make the choice.

885
00:46:59,733 --> 00:47:00,651
Seriously.

886
00:47:05,614 --> 00:47:07,032
Maybe I'll make a move on you next.

887
00:47:07,115 --> 00:47:08,659
Like, "What about me?"

888
00:47:09,827 --> 00:47:11,203
"Take a good look at me."

889
00:47:18,627 --> 00:47:19,586
Hey, Bo!

890
00:47:19,670 --> 00:47:20,921
Get lost, man. Not now.

891
00:47:21,004 --> 00:47:23,215
- Come on, Bo.
- Don't get nervous, dumbass.

892
00:47:23,298 --> 00:47:24,591
You could tell?

893
00:47:24,675 --> 00:47:25,759
Bo! Bo!

894
00:47:30,514 --> 00:47:31,890
I don't know what I should do.

895
00:47:33,600 --> 00:47:35,227
Have you decided who your top choice is?

896
00:47:36,937 --> 00:47:38,063
Hmm…

897
00:47:39,022 --> 00:47:41,275
Honestly, you don't have to hold back
to protect me.

898
00:47:41,358 --> 00:47:42,985
I know. I'm not holding back.

899
00:47:43,068 --> 00:47:46,280
- If it's Ari, then fine. I can back off.
- That's not it. I swear.

900
00:47:46,363 --> 00:47:47,990
I can wave the white flag. Why not?

901
00:47:48,073 --> 00:47:49,616
Wouldn't it be better if you just said

902
00:47:49,700 --> 00:47:51,535
- what you feel?
- Wait. That's not it.

903
00:47:51,618 --> 00:47:54,037
If I'd made up my mind,
I would just tell you.

904
00:47:56,707 --> 00:47:59,543
I keep thinking maybe
I should give up on you, Hikaru.

905
00:47:59,626 --> 00:48:01,962
- But the thing is--
- Then maybe we should start from scratch.

906
00:48:02,754 --> 00:48:05,007
Okay, but, even if we start from scratch,

907
00:48:05,090 --> 00:48:07,384
there's no one else
I'm interested in anymore.

908
00:48:08,427 --> 00:48:09,553
It's only you.

909
00:48:13,932 --> 00:48:16,602
Once I decide someone is the one,
that's it for me.

910
00:48:18,979 --> 00:48:21,106
But I don't want to force you to choose.

911
00:48:25,235 --> 00:48:27,446
- Someone said the same thing to him.
- Exactly.

912
00:48:27,529 --> 00:48:29,531
You should know better than anyone
how it feels.

913
00:48:32,826 --> 00:48:34,912
All right. Did you read it?

914
00:48:35,412 --> 00:48:37,080
- Hmm? Oh, yeah.
- You did?

915
00:48:37,164 --> 00:48:39,291
Thanks for writing it.
It was nice to hear.

916
00:48:39,374 --> 00:48:40,375
It made me happy.

917
00:48:41,043 --> 00:48:42,711
Yeah, yeah. Nice.

918
00:48:42,794 --> 00:48:45,005
Can I talk to you
whenever you guys are done?

919
00:48:45,088 --> 00:48:46,798
- Sure.
- <i>Oh, Ha-chan.</i>

920
00:48:46,882 --> 00:48:48,759
- Is that okay?
- It's okay.

921
00:48:49,927 --> 00:48:51,386
- See ya.
- Yeah, see ya.

922
00:48:52,554 --> 00:48:55,057
- That was quick.
- Huh?

923
00:48:55,140 --> 00:48:57,726
We don't have anything
we need to talk out.

924
00:48:57,809 --> 00:49:01,521
- Don't say there's nothing to talk about.
- Whoa, no! We can talk about stuff.

925
00:49:01,605 --> 00:49:03,982
That's not what I meant!
Sorry, I misspoke.

926
00:49:05,192 --> 00:49:06,026
See ya.

927
00:49:06,109 --> 00:49:08,403
That's a part of his personality, right?
His way with words?

928
00:49:08,487 --> 00:49:11,114
He says just a bit too much.
He's clumsy with words.

929
00:49:11,198 --> 00:49:12,658
Lots of people talk like that.

930
00:49:12,741 --> 00:49:15,118
- Yeah, they do.
- Don't you think?

931
00:49:15,202 --> 00:49:16,036
What's up?

932
00:49:17,037 --> 00:49:17,955
- Hear me out.
- Okay.

933
00:49:18,038 --> 00:49:20,916
- I've finally found someone I like.
- Yeah, I figured as much.

934
00:49:20,999 --> 00:49:22,000
It's Tai-chan.

935
00:49:22,501 --> 00:49:24,044
- How did you know?
- Hmm?

936
00:49:24,544 --> 00:49:25,545
- Tai-chan?
- Huh?

937
00:49:27,130 --> 00:49:29,591
I was staring at Tai-chan's face
for a long time.

938
00:49:29,675 --> 00:49:32,761
And the more I stared, the more
I was like, "Wow, he's good-looking."

939
00:49:32,844 --> 00:49:34,805
Get out of here!

940
00:49:35,389 --> 00:49:36,723
Tai-chan is so popular.

941
00:49:36,807 --> 00:49:39,810
And then I felt
a little flutter in my heart.

942
00:49:39,893 --> 00:49:43,230
I see. You're being so romantic, Ha-chan.

943
00:49:44,189 --> 00:49:47,192
I've never had a romance
that started with me saying,

944
00:49:47,275 --> 00:49:50,320
"Hey, look, I'm interested in you."

945
00:49:50,404 --> 00:49:53,490
To be honest,
the only guys I've ever dated

946
00:49:53,573 --> 00:49:57,494
were just customers who used
to request me, back when I was working,

947
00:49:58,161 --> 00:49:59,496
in the nightlife industry.

948
00:50:00,038 --> 00:50:01,540
For me, I have to prepare myself

949
00:50:01,623 --> 00:50:03,917
for taking the initiative
with someone I like.

950
00:50:04,960 --> 00:50:07,879
In kickboxing, if you step into
the ring and just freeze,

951
00:50:08,672 --> 00:50:09,506
it's over.

952
00:50:10,257 --> 00:50:13,260
Mmm, this is honestly
the first real challenge of my life.

953
00:50:15,387 --> 00:50:17,556
- Good morning.
- Morning, everyone.

954
00:50:17,639 --> 00:50:19,057
What are we making?

955
00:50:19,141 --> 00:50:20,684
- Omelet rice.
- For real?

956
00:50:20,767 --> 00:50:21,852
There's a ritual.

957
00:50:21,935 --> 00:50:23,645
- What? A ritual?
- What ritual?

958
00:50:23,729 --> 00:50:25,564
- A ketchup ritual?
- Eggs are here.

959
00:50:25,647 --> 00:50:27,274
- A ketchup writing ritual?
- You're right.

960
00:50:27,357 --> 00:50:28,734
This is important.

961
00:50:28,817 --> 00:50:31,528
- This is an important moment, you idiot!
- It's a big deal.

962
00:50:31,611 --> 00:50:32,863
Looks delicious.

963
00:50:32,946 --> 00:50:35,782
Ketchup on omelet and rice
is every guy's dream.

964
00:50:35,866 --> 00:50:37,743
- Yeah.
- Right?

965
00:50:37,826 --> 00:50:39,911
Looks like you girls got
the ketchup under control.

966
00:50:39,995 --> 00:50:41,747
We'll leave it to you. Thank you.

967
00:50:41,830 --> 00:50:44,166
- Good work.
- Nice. How many guys are there?

968
00:50:44,249 --> 00:50:45,333
We need six, yeah?

969
00:50:46,043 --> 00:50:47,794
I'll do Ma-kun's. Yeah?

970
00:50:48,962 --> 00:50:51,506
- Yeah, that works.
- I'm gonna write "Masaya" here.

971
00:50:51,590 --> 00:50:53,550
Isn't that hard? You're good.

972
00:50:53,633 --> 00:50:56,845
- Oh, cute.
- <i>Oh, cute. She's good.</i>

973
00:50:56,928 --> 00:50:58,055
<i>He's gonna like that.</i>

974
00:50:58,638 --> 00:50:59,890
- You writing Ari's?
- Yeah.

975
00:51:00,682 --> 00:51:02,309
- Tai-chan's?
- I want to write on Tai-chan's.

976
00:51:02,392 --> 00:51:03,935
- Is that okay?
- Yeah, why not?

977
00:51:04,019 --> 00:51:05,645
- And you?
- You're writing on Leo's?

978
00:51:05,729 --> 00:51:07,647
Leo's and Kazu-kun's. Who do you want?

979
00:51:07,731 --> 00:51:09,900
It's fine. I won't write on anyone's.

980
00:51:09,983 --> 00:51:12,486
- You sure?
- Are you sure? That could change things.

981
00:51:12,569 --> 00:51:15,030
- It's a good time to make a choice.
- Mmm.

982
00:51:15,113 --> 00:51:17,157
This ketchup could change
the course of history.

983
00:51:17,240 --> 00:51:19,576
Is this ketchup
a matter of life and death?

984
00:51:19,659 --> 00:51:22,454
"This ketchup could change
the course of history."

985
00:51:22,537 --> 00:51:24,664
I've never heard anyone
phrase it like that.

986
00:51:24,748 --> 00:51:26,083
It could change the situation.

987
00:51:26,166 --> 00:51:28,043
- Will we tell them who wrote the names?
- Yeah.

988
00:51:28,543 --> 00:51:31,505
- Whose name do you want to write the most?
- Wait. I don't like this.

989
00:51:32,005 --> 00:51:34,091
Seriously.
Whose name do you want to write?

990
00:51:34,174 --> 00:51:35,926
If there's overlap,
we'll do rock-paper-scissors.

991
00:51:36,009 --> 00:51:37,969
- Can I just pass on writing?
- You can't.

992
00:51:38,678 --> 00:51:41,306
But then I could end up
misleading them again.

993
00:51:41,389 --> 00:51:42,974
- Then communicate that to them.
- I did.

994
00:51:43,058 --> 00:51:44,768
I told them I haven't decided.

995
00:51:44,851 --> 00:51:47,813
Okay, but still,
one of them has to stand out more.

996
00:51:47,896 --> 00:51:50,398
It's not like you feel nothing
for them, equally.

997
00:51:50,482 --> 00:51:52,901
You have some feelings
for one of them, at least.

998
00:51:52,984 --> 00:51:55,112
Who do you feel the strongest for, Hikaru?

999
00:51:57,072 --> 00:51:58,907
I'm serious. It's both of them.

1000
00:52:00,951 --> 00:52:02,369
You've got to make up your mind.

1001
00:52:02,452 --> 00:52:04,496
- Otherwise, we can't decide either.
- They need to know.

1002
00:52:13,130 --> 00:52:15,173
- This is hard.
- Just go for it.

1003
00:52:16,133 --> 00:52:17,050
Oh, this is bad!

1004
00:52:19,094 --> 00:52:20,303
It's so bad!

1005
00:52:20,387 --> 00:52:21,680
It's terrible!

1006
00:52:21,763 --> 00:52:23,932
So bad.

1007
00:52:24,015 --> 00:52:25,350
That looks good.

1008
00:52:27,185 --> 00:52:29,229
I'll put a smiley face on Kazu-kun's.

1009
00:52:29,312 --> 00:52:30,313
Yeah.

1010
00:52:34,860 --> 00:52:37,487
- Cute.
- Does that mean I'm bad at it?

1011
00:52:37,571 --> 00:52:40,949
- No. I meant it's cute.
- Oop! Beep, beep! You're too nice!

1012
00:52:41,032 --> 00:52:42,868
Okay. Should we go?

1013
00:52:42,951 --> 00:52:45,996
I meant "cute" literally.
I didn't know it would sound so loaded.

1014
00:52:46,079 --> 00:52:47,080
Let's go.

1015
00:52:47,164 --> 00:52:48,623
Just kidding. Thanks, Ha-chan.

1016
00:52:48,707 --> 00:52:50,584
Maririn, you want to write
on Ari's, right?

1017
00:52:50,667 --> 00:52:52,502
- Yeah.
- That's fine.

1018
00:52:53,253 --> 00:52:54,838
I'll just write on Bo's.

1019
00:52:54,921 --> 00:52:56,590
- Okay.
- He's my bestie.

1020
00:52:58,341 --> 00:53:00,427
- Hmm.
- Should I write "Wassup"?

1021
00:53:00,969 --> 00:53:02,596
Can you write "Wassup"?

1022
00:53:04,598 --> 00:53:07,559
- How are you so good at that?
- I used to work at a cafe.

1023
00:53:07,642 --> 00:53:10,020
- Oh, that explains it! You're good.
- Really? Whoa!

1024
00:53:12,397 --> 00:53:15,025
If you squeeze it slowly,
it works better. Here.

1025
00:53:15,108 --> 00:53:17,152
- Got it.
- So cute.

1026
00:53:17,235 --> 00:53:20,447
- I'm like a school teacher.
- I think it's cute.

1027
00:53:20,530 --> 00:53:23,491
- Is that the "earth" radical?
- And "direction" on the right.

1028
00:53:24,451 --> 00:53:25,785
Oh, you're good.

1029
00:53:27,329 --> 00:53:29,372
Wow, look at that.

1030
00:53:29,456 --> 00:53:30,707
A work of art.

1031
00:53:30,790 --> 00:53:31,625
BO

1032
00:53:31,708 --> 00:53:34,085
Wait, what does this mean?
What's her deal?

1033
00:53:34,169 --> 00:53:36,046
She's writing on Bo's
because they're just friends.

1034
00:53:36,129 --> 00:53:38,840
No way, Bo's gonna
totally misinterpret that.

1035
00:53:38,924 --> 00:53:42,052
I think she's completely lost
at this point, even to herself.

1036
00:53:42,636 --> 00:53:44,638
- It's ready.
- Hooray!

1037
00:53:44,721 --> 00:53:45,639
Hey!

1038
00:53:47,474 --> 00:53:48,433
Let's eat.

1039
00:53:50,060 --> 00:53:52,187
This is for Tai-chan. I did the ketchup.

1040
00:53:52,270 --> 00:53:54,564
I wasn't sure what to write,
so I drew a face.

1041
00:53:54,648 --> 00:53:56,191
<i>She's making her move on Tai-chan.</i>

1042
00:53:56,274 --> 00:53:57,734
- Is this mine? Thanks.
- Yeah.

1043
00:53:57,817 --> 00:53:59,569
- It's cute, right?
- Hell yeah!

1044
00:53:59,653 --> 00:54:01,071
Here you go, Kazuma.

1045
00:54:02,948 --> 00:54:03,782
Thank you.

1046
00:54:04,366 --> 00:54:05,533
- Wassup.
- Oh, thanks.

1047
00:54:05,617 --> 00:54:06,993
- Here.
- Wassup! You're good!

1048
00:54:07,077 --> 00:54:07,911
WASSUP

1049
00:54:07,994 --> 00:54:09,246
- Great work.
- You like it?

1050
00:54:09,329 --> 00:54:11,498
- Look at this.
- Awesome!

1051
00:54:11,581 --> 00:54:12,540
It's a heart!

1052
00:54:12,624 --> 00:54:13,583
MASAYA

1053
00:54:13,667 --> 00:54:16,378
- Hey, Assun, take a picture, will you?
- This is great!

1054
00:54:16,461 --> 00:54:17,712
Here we go.

1055
00:54:17,796 --> 00:54:19,881
- Okay, say cheese.
- <i>So cute! </i>

1056
00:54:19,965 --> 00:54:21,132
<i>They're into this, huh?</i>

1057
00:54:21,216 --> 00:54:22,801
- Okay, let's go!
- Yay!

1058
00:54:22,884 --> 00:54:23,760
BO

1059
00:54:23,843 --> 00:54:25,387
- Does this mean glutton?
- Huh?

1060
00:54:25,470 --> 00:54:27,597
Or, "spoiled brat."

1061
00:54:29,015 --> 00:54:30,892
Just for now. It can never go public.

1062
00:54:31,977 --> 00:54:34,396
- Hey, we did great. Let's eat.
- Dig in!

1063
00:54:34,479 --> 00:54:36,064
- Ooh, yeah.
- Let's eat!

1064
00:54:37,065 --> 00:54:38,942
- Looks delicious.
- I want a bite of that too.

1065
00:54:39,025 --> 00:54:39,859
Sure.

1066
00:54:39,943 --> 00:54:42,320
- It's about to be gone.
- What do you mean?

1067
00:54:42,404 --> 00:54:44,114
- That's funny.
- Yeah.

1068
00:54:44,197 --> 00:54:46,199
- That photo is so good.
- This is delicious.

1069
00:54:46,283 --> 00:54:47,117
It is.

1070
00:54:47,200 --> 00:54:50,203
In terms of our time spent together,
we're about halfway.

1071
00:54:50,287 --> 00:54:52,706
- Less than half, actually.
- Let's give it our all.

1072
00:54:54,332 --> 00:54:57,043
- We should be like Usain Bolt.
- What's that mean?

1073
00:54:57,127 --> 00:54:59,838
Go full speed! Whoosh! Bah!

1074
00:54:59,921 --> 00:55:01,923
- Back to his old self.
- Full of energy.

1075
00:55:02,007 --> 00:55:03,967
- Usain Bolt.
- Like, bam!

1076
00:55:05,385 --> 00:55:07,095
- We're still eating.
- I knew this was coming.

1077
00:55:08,722 --> 00:55:11,141
- I have a bad feeling about this.
- Hmm?

1078
00:55:11,224 --> 00:55:12,976
- <i>It's sauna time.</i>
- Yay.

1079
00:55:13,059 --> 00:55:13,977
Sauna?

1080
00:55:14,060 --> 00:55:15,729
- Pick Bo.
<i>- The person who gets</i>

1081
00:55:15,812 --> 00:55:19,649
<i>to choose today is someone</i>
<i>who hasn't been in the sauna yet.</i>

1082
00:55:20,692 --> 00:55:22,402
- It's Hikaru.
<i>- It's me.</i>

1083
00:55:22,485 --> 00:55:23,653
<i>Hikaru!</i>

1084
00:55:23,737 --> 00:55:27,782
<i>You may now choose the man</i>
<i>that you'd like to go in the sauna with.</i>

1085
00:55:39,753 --> 00:55:40,587
Okay.

1086
00:55:41,755 --> 00:55:42,756
I've decided.

1087
00:55:49,054 --> 00:55:49,888
Ari.

1088
00:55:50,472 --> 00:55:51,890
- Eh?
- Eh?

1089
00:55:56,644 --> 00:55:57,729
It's sauna time.
